module gunbc.shared_fill_attribution_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust added by splitting shared-artifact fill cost out of
// a claim's measured CPU. Authored because gunbc.seed_growth_admission
// seed_growth_forward_freeze_policy_note makes unenumerated hand growth in src/v1 a stop-line,
// and this change adds two hand items to v1_compiler.cli_run.
//
// WHAT THE CHANGE IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. It is an ATTRIBUTION correction on an existing
// measurement, not a new budget, exemption or tolerance. run_claim_measured already measured a
// claim's CPU and already compared it to required_floor_claim_cpu_safety_limit_ms; this branch
// changes WHICH WORK that number covers and changes neither the limit nor its fail-stop
// semantics. Measured against the merge base, the whole cli_run delta is 72 added lines.
//
// WHY IT WAS ADDED. The memoized compile_dag_rust_emit_check is a SHARED artifact: the first
// claim to reach a given source pays the whole compile and every later claim reads it for free.
// Charging that fill to whichever claim happened to arrive first bills one row for work the
// roster shares, so the row's reported cost is a function of DISCOVERY ORDER rather than of the
// row -- and the safety limit is a FAIL-STOP protecting the executor, so an order-dependent
// number decides whether the line stops. The floor already carries the vocabulary for this: it
// bills a shared build to preparation via SharedBuildProvenance, and this reuses that framing
// rather than minting a second one (operator ruling on gunbc#9477 -- reuse the existing
// provenance field rather than inventing an exemption).
//
// THE FORCING CLASS IS THE DISCRIMINATOR, AND THE THIRD STATE IS THE DEFECT. A shared artifact
// is in one of two arms depending on WHEN it can be forced, and the arm decides its treatment:
//
//   PREPARATION-FORCEABLE -- every identity it can be asked for is knowable before the fold, so
//     the floor BUILDS it ahead and bills preparation. both_closure_edge_index is this arm:
//     run_required_floor warms it over both index identities its resolves can reach, and the run
//     reports provenance=built-by-preparation. No claim window ever contains that build, which is
//     why it correctly carries no fill bracket -- absence of a bracket is not evidence of a defect
//     here, and reasoning from that absence is what this receipt exists to stop.
//
//   CLAIM-FORCED -- what it will be asked for is a property of the claim, so it CANNOT be warmed
//     ahead. A witness's synthetic source is not knowable before the fold. This arm must record
//     its fill through record_shared_artifact_fill_cpu so run_claim_measured charges the marginal
//     half and reports the shared half.
//
// THE THIRD STATE MUST NOT EXIST: claim-forced and unbracketed. Its cost lands entirely on
// whichever claim arrives first, and the number it produces is REAL -- a true measurement of
// something, charged to a row that does not own it -- so nothing looks wrong. The census memo was
// in this state from gunbc#9428 until this change, and it refused the required floor at 5812ms
// against a 5000ms fail-stop while two later claims read the same compiles free. The danger is
// worse than a wrong number: gunbc#9517 proposes freezing rows above the line in a shrink-only
// contract, and a row frozen for cost it does not own can never be made cheap, so it can never
// leave. A miswarded measurement becomes permanent.
//
// THIS PROSE IS NOT A WALL, AND SAYING SO IS PART OF THE ROW (DESIGN section 4b(1) -- the reported
// rung must be the rung executed evidence establishes). The two treatments are two hand-written
// call sites with no carrier relating them, so "claim-forced and unbracketed" stays WRITABLE and
// nothing refuses it; the next memo reintroduces the defect and this paragraph will not stop it.
// RUNG: mitigatable, on review diligence. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a memoized host artifact DECLARES its
// forcing class and the warm-or-net treatment is DERIVED from that declaration, at which point the
// third state has no spelling and the bracket cannot be forgotten. That is a construction this
// change does not make and does not claim.
//
// THE TRIGGER ABOVE IS NO LONGER THIS FILE'S TO CARRY, AND THIS PARAGRAPH RETIRES IT AS AN
// AUTHORITY WHILE LEAVING THE REASONING IT SITS BESIDE INTACT. The class is now filed as
// gunbc.recurring_failure_mode `claim_forced_and_unbracketed`, which is a TYPED CARRIER a fold can
// read; these lines are a section 4c annotation, which no Accepted program can. Two statements of
// one trigger in two places is the section 3 fork, and the one that survives is the one something
// can consume -- so the row is the trigger's home and the wording above is kept only as the
// rationale for why this change has the shape it does. If the two ever disagree, the row wins.
//
// WHY IT IS RUST AND NOT .dag. The measured subject is a host builtin. compile_dag_rust_emit_check
// runs the seed compiler synchronously and its memo lives beside it, so the fill interval exists
// only inside the host call; the substrate has no representation of that call to time. A
// .dag-side accounting would have to attribute an interval it cannot observe, which is a layer
// inversion rather than a migration -- the same boundary gunbc.census_memo_seed_growth records
// one seam over, and the two dissolve together for the same reason.
//
// WHAT IS NOT NETTED. run_claim_measured is ExistingSeedItemModified per
// gunbc.seed_growth_admission SeedGrowthChangeDisposition -- it keeps its name and signature --
// so it is not counted as an addition.
//
// HAND-ITEM DELTA: +2 citable declarations, both in v1_compiler.cli_run. One module-level
// thread-local accumulator is added and is NOT a citable declaration; it is named here rather
// than omitted, because a receipt that counts only what the roster can cite would under-report
// its own growth.
data shared_fill_attribution_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "record_shared_artifact_fill_cpu", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "shared_artifact_fill_cpu_nanos", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "Accounting for a host-side shared artifact is a property of the host that fills it. record_shared_artifact_fill_cpu accumulates the interval a MISS spent filling a shared memoized host compile -- the emit-check memo and its census sibling both call it, because one accounting rule with two homes must be applied in both; shared_artifact_fill_cpu_nanos reads that accumulator so run_claim_measured can subtract the shared half from the claim's own. Both exist because the two halves must be read at the same seam: a total with no split is the order-dependent number this change exists to remove.\n\nWHICH ARTIFACTS MUST CALL IT is decided by forcing class, stated in this file's header: an artifact the floor can warm ahead of the fold is billed to preparation and needs no bracket, and an artifact only a claim can force must record its fill here. An artifact in neither arm is the defect, and it is a state this receipt describes rather than forbids -- the relation between the two treatments is prose, not a carrier, so nothing refuses a memo that declares no class.\n\nENUMERATED RATHER THAN COUNTED. Both are free functions, so the citable count and the real count are both two; nothing lands in seed_growth_uncitable_item_keys. The added thread-local is not a declaration and is disclosed in this file's header instead.\n\nTHE SPLIT IS REPORTED, NOT SILENTLY APPLIED. Every claim whose fill interval is nonzero emits a [floor-shared-fill] line naming the claim, its marginal CPU, the fill CPU and the measured total, so the subtraction is visible in the run that made it and can be disagreed with. A subtraction that only ever shrank a number without saying so would be an unaccounted widening of the safety limit -- the absorbing-fallback shape DESIGN section 5 forbids -- and the line is what keeps it a measurement instead.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete both when compile_dag_rust_emit_check and its census sibling are MODELED operations rather than host builtins -- at which point the shared artifact is the substrate's own Realization on a content hash, its fill is an ordinary node the cost model already sees, and attributing it by hand is the duplicated accounting authority that carrier dissolves. This receipt and gunbc.census_memo_seed_growth retire in the same change or neither does: they are the cache and the bill for one artifact, and separating them would leave a hand-rolled accounting beside a modeled one.",
  current_boundary: "Confined to one process and one call site pair. The accumulator is thread-local, is written only on a shared-memo MISS -- the emit-check memo and its census sibling, which are the two memoized host compiles the floor arms -- and is read only by run_claim_measured, so nothing outside the required floor observes it. It changes no verdict for any claim that fills nothing: with a zero fill interval the subtraction is the identity and no line is emitted. What it does change is a claim that pays for a shared compile, which is the whole point -- and the value it reports is the claim's own marginal cost, never a reduced form of the shared cost, which is still paid and still measured."
}
